# Data Science Jobs Analysis Using R

## 📌 Project Overview

This project focuses on analyzing a dataset of **Data Science job postings** using **R**.

The project covers the main steps of the data analysis process, starting with **data cleaning and preparation**, followed by **Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)** to better understand the dataset and extract useful insights about Data Science job opportunities.

This project was completed as part of my training at **NTI – National Telecommunication Institute**.

---

## 🎯 Project Objectives

The main objectives of this project were to:

* Clean and prepare the dataset for analysis.
* Handle inconsistencies in job titles and company names.
* Explore the distribution of different Data Science job roles.
* Analyze job locations, industries, and sectors.
* Explore salary estimates and company ratings.
* Identify patterns and trends within the job market.
* Practice data cleaning and exploratory analysis using R.

---

## 🗂️ Dataset

The dataset contains information about Data Science-related job postings, including:

* Job Title
* Salary Estimate
* Job Description
* Company Name
* Company Rating
* Location
* Headquarters
* Company Size
* Founded Year
* Type of Ownership
* Industry
* Sector
* Revenue
* Competitors

The dataset required several cleaning steps before it could be used for analysis, especially for fields such as **Job Title** and **Company Name**.

---

## 🧹 Data Cleaning

The data cleaning stage included:

* Inspecting the dataset structure and columns.
* Checking and handling inconsistencies in the data.
* Cleaning **Job Titles** and standardizing similar job title variations.
* Cleaning **Company Names** by removing unnecessary information that was included with the company names.
* Preparing categorical columns for further analysis.
* Checking the cleaned values and reviewing unique categories.

The goal was to make the dataset more consistent and suitable for the analysis stage.

---

## 📊 Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

After cleaning the dataset, I performed **Exploratory Data Analysis** to understand the main patterns in the data.

The analysis included exploring:

* Most common Data Science job titles.
* Job locations.
* Industries and sectors.
* Salary estimates.
* Company ratings.
* Different companies hiring for Data Science-related roles.
* Skills and requirements mentioned in job descriptions.

One of the observations from the analysis was that **Data Scientist** was one of the most frequently occurring job titles in the dataset.

